This directory contains the source code for third-party libraries
vendored by RT. The contents below are generated from the per-library
metadata.yml files; see SCHEMA.md for the field reference. Do not edit
this file by hand -- run devel/tools/generate-third-party-readme --write
to regenerate.

* bootstrap/ (5.3.1)
Description: Front-end framework for building responsive, mobile-first web
  sites.
Origin: https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap
License: MIT
Note:
  RT uses the non-bundle build of Bootstrap (bootstrap.js / bootstrap.min.js
  rather than bootstrap.bundle.* ), because Popper is vendored separately
  under devel/third-party/popper/.

* bootstrap-combobox/ (1.2.0)
Description: Combobox widget for Bootstrap, adding autocomplete behavior to
  <select>.
Origin: https://github.com/danielfarrell/bootstrap-combobox
License: Apache-2.0
Note:
  The scoped npm package @danielfarrell/bootstrap-combobox stops at 1.1.8;
  the 1.2.0 we ship corresponds to the upstream GitHub release tag of the
  same number and was never published to npm. The purl uses the GitHub
  form so advisory lookups resolve against the actual artifact we ship.

* bootstrap-icons/ (1.10.3)
Description: Official open source SVG icon library for Bootstrap with over
  1,900 icons.
Origin: https://github.com/twbs/icons
License: MIT
Note:
  Unlike the other entries under devel/third-party/, this directory holds
  only metadata. The icons themselves are individual SVG files under
  share/static/images/, selected per %SVG in etc/RT_Config.pm.in.

* chart-js-4/ (4.4.7)
Description: HTML5 charts using the <canvas> tag.
Origin: https://github.com/chartjs/Chart.js
License: MIT

* chartjs-plugin-colorschemes/ (0.6.4)
Description: Predefined color schemes for Chart.js.
Origin: https://github.com/MaximBelov/chartjs-plugin-colorschemes
License: MIT
Note:
  This is the maintained MaximBelov fork of the original (inactive)
  nagix/chartjs-plugin-colorschemes project.

* ckeditor5/ (44.2.0)
Description: WYSIWYG rich-text editor. Parses and renders user-supplied HTML,
  so any vulnerability here is a direct XSS exposure in RT's ticket UI.
Origin: https://github.com/ckeditor/ckeditor5
License: GPL-2.0-or-later
Note:
  Plugin selection is controlled at runtime via the
  %MessageBoxRichTextInitArguments configuration variable in RT, not by
  customizing the build. The emoji feature additionally requires
  share/static/RichText5/en.json (or other locale file), fetched separately
  from `https://cdn.ckeditor.com/ckeditor5/data/emoji/<n>/` -- this is under
  the same GPL-2.0-or-later license as CKEditor itself. See README for
  the upstream issue tracking native packaging of that file.
  Dual-license note: CKSource offers CKEditor 5 under either GPL-2.0-or-later
  or a commercial license. RT uses the GPL option, so we keep both
  COPYING.GPL (the actual GPL v2 text) and LICENSE.md (the upstream summary
  that describes the dual-license arrangement and lists embedded third-party
  components and their licenses).

* cytoscape/ (3.33.4)
Description: Graph theory (network) library for visualization and analysis.
Origin: https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape.js
License: MIT

* dropzone-7/ (7.2.0)
Description: Drag-and-drop file upload widget. Handles user-provided files,
  making it a security-relevant entry point.
Origin: https://github.com/NicolasCARPi/dropzone
License: MIT
Note:
  This is the maintained NicolasCARPi fork of the original (inactive)
  enyo/dropzone project. The post-copy step "remove the sourceMappingURL
  comment from dropzone.css and dropzone.min.js" is documented in the README.

* htmx/ (2.0.3)
Description: Access to AJAX, CSS transitions, WebSockets and Server-Sent
  Events directly in HTML via element attributes. Drives a lot of RT's modern
  interactivity.
Origin: https://github.com/bigskysoftware/htmx
License: 0BSD

* jquery/ (3.6.0)
Description: DOM manipulation, event handling, and AJAX helpers. Foundational
  JS dependency used throughout RT's UI.
Origin: https://github.com/jquery/jquery
License: MIT
Note:
  Single-file library: the upstream source jquery-3.6.0.js lives in this
  directory; the minified copy shipped to clients lives separately under
  share/static/js/.

* jquery-jgrowl/ (1.4.10)
Description: JavaScript notification system providing growl-style messages.
Origin: https://github.com/stanlemon/jGrowl
License: MIT
Note:
  The banner inside jquery.jgrowl.js says "jGrowl 1.4.5" even at the upstream
  1.4.10 tag -- the author cut the 1.4.10 release without bumping the in-file
  version string. The 1.4.10 recorded here tracks the upstream release tag,
  which is what advisory databases reference.

* jquery-tablesorter/ (2.0.5b)
Description: Client-side sortable HTML tables without page refresh.
Origin: https://github.com/christianbach/tablesorter
License: MIT
Note:
  Single-file library. The original project (christianbach) is no longer
  actively maintained; the Mottie/tablesorter fork is the current home of
  this code on npm but RT has not migrated to it.
  Upstream ships no standalone LICENSE file; the file in this directory
  was reconstructed from the source-file header in jquery.tablesorter.js,
  which declares: "Copyright (c) 2007 Christian Bach. Dual licensed under
  the MIT and GPL licenses." RT uses this code under the MIT half of that
  offer (SPDX: MIT).

* mousetrap/ (1.5.3)
Description: Library for binding keyboard shortcuts.
Origin: https://github.com/ccampbell/mousetrap
License: Apache-2.0
Note:
  Single-file library. The upstream project has been minimally maintained
  for years; consider auditing for an actively-maintained alternative if
  a CVE lands.

* popper/ (2.11.8)
Description: Tooltip and popover positioning engine.
Origin: https://github.com/floating-ui/floating-ui
License: MIT
Note:
  Popper.js v2 was superseded by Floating UI in the same repository; the
  @popperjs/core npm package is the still-published v2 line.

* tempus-dominus/ (6.9.4)
Description: Powerful and flexible date/time picker widget.
Origin: https://github.com/Eonasdan/tempus-dominus
License: MIT

* tom-select/ (2.5.2)
Description: A modern select with autocomplete and native-feeling keyboard
  navigation.
Origin: https://github.com/orchidjs/tom-select
License: Apache-2.0
